===Etymology===
{{prefix|un|paid|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|/ʌnˈpeɪd/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪd|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|un|paid|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not [[paid]] for.
#: {{ux|en|an '''unpaid''' bill}}
# Of work: done without [[agreed]] [[payment]], usually [[voluntarily]].
#: {{ux|en|an '''unpaid''' position}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Hisham S. El-Osta|author2=Mary C. Ahearn|chapter=Introduction|title=Estimating the Opportunity Cost of Unpaid Farm Labor for U.S. Farm Operators|series=Technical Bulletin|seriesvolume=no. 1848|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher={{w|Economic Research Service}}, {{w|United States Department of Agriculture}}|month=March|year=1996|page=1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ucJDAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA1|oclc=37447588|passage=Farm labor is a critical input in agricultural production. Farm operators provide just about half of all labor hours in agriculture, most of which are '''unpaid'''. An additional 18 percent of farm labor hours are '''unpaid''' hours provided by farm household members, partners, and others.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=[[w:United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific|Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific]], {{w|United Nations Development Programme}}|chapter=Introduction|title=Integrating Unpaid Work into National Policies|series=sales no. E.03.II.F.14|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|United Nations}}|year=2003|pages=7–8|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-uUtRRL8biAC&pg=PA|isbn=978-92-1-120151-2|passage=[A]ll people who perform work, paid or '''unpaid''', are economically active. It is, and always has been, quite misleading to regard people who perform only '''unpaid''' household work outside the SNA &#91;{{w|United Nations System of National Accounts}}&#93; production boundary as economically inactive.}}

